# KiCad per-user files, caches, backups and lock files
*.kicad_prl
fp-info-cache
*-backups/
*.lck
~*.lck
_autosave-*
*-cache.lib
# MCP server reports written next to the board
*_drc_violations.json

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# PCB generator scratch (regenerate with pcb/tools/generate.py, then pcb/tools/make_outputs.py).
# pcb/production/ (fab files, BOMs, STEP) and pcb/docs/ (PDFs, renders, reports) are generated too, but they are KEPT.
# Note: the housing build reads pcb/build/geometry.json, so run the PCB step before housing/src/build.py.
pcb/build/

# Housing build outputs (regenerate with housing/src/build.py).
# KEPT: housing/out/print/ (print files), housing/out/render/ (renders), REPORT.md, checks.json and the slice-report JSONs.
housing/out/E/
housing/out/slice/*/
# OrcaSlicer / OCC logs
**/00000.log

# Local fit-reference copy of the separate silkscreen-enclosure-claude repository (rev K, about 271 MB).
# The housing checks read the stock case from here. It belongs to that repo: copy it in from there, never commit it.
enclosures/silkscreen-enclosure-claude/

# Local only, never published (2026-10-21): agent notes with machine paths, the workflow scripts that drove the
# design runs (machine paths), third-party evidence (a datasheet page, LCSC/EasyEDA part data), rev A build logs
# with machine paths, and slicer G-code.
CLAUDE.local.md
workflows/
pcb/docs/sources/
archive/rev-A-rod-lens/pcb/docs/sources/
archive/rev-A-rod-lens/housing/out/*.log
archive/rev-A-rod-lens/housing/out/E/
archive/rev-A-rod-lens/housing/out/slice/*/
*.gcode
